Scope and third-party components

MIT is the license of the first-party sources in this folder. It matches the
`SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT` header carried by every first-party Solidity
file under `contracts/src`, `contracts/test` and `contracts/script`; this file
is the license those headers refer to. The first-party sources that carry no
per-file header - the TypeScript under `circuits/` and `scripts/`, the circom
sources under `circuits/src/card/`, and the shell/PowerShell build scripts -
are covered by this file directly.

Two sets of files in this folder are NOT covered by the grant above and keep
the license their own headers state:

1. Vendored upstream dependencies under `contracts/lib/`, preserved
   byte-for-byte at the commits pinned by `contracts/risc0-ethereum.lock.json`
   and verified by `scripts/verify-artifact-locks.mjs`:

   - `contracts/lib/risc0-ethereum/` - RISC Zero, Inc., Apache-2.0
   - `contracts/lib/openzeppelin-compat/`,
     `contracts/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/`,
     `contracts/lib/openzeppelin-contracts-upgradeable/` - OpenZeppelin, MIT
   - `contracts/lib/forge-std/` - Foundry, dual MIT / Apache-2.0

2. Groth16 verifier sources generated by snarkJS, which emits its own GPL-3.0
   header (Copyright 2021 0KIMS association):

   - `circuits/card-verifiers/CardDeckInitGroth16VerifierV4.sol`
   - `circuits/card-verifiers/CardHandActionGroth16VerifierV4.sol`
   - `contracts/src/l2/v5/generated/CardDeckInitGroth16VerifierV5.sol`
   - `contracts/src/l2/v5/generated/CardHandActionGroth16VerifierV5.sol`
   - the same two files regenerated under `circuits/build/card/`

   These are the demo-only hidden-card circuits (uncontributed phase-2 keys).
   They are not part of the rollup's proof path.

The zkdeal prover source in the sibling `prover-node/` folder is published
separately under the Business Source License 1.1
(`prover-node/zkdeal-BUSL-1.1-LICENSE`) and is not covered by this file.
